# @container/runtime — runtime backend species (process-side).
# Arc 5 TICK 5 GREEN landing per Reed RED at `2a5c7ad` against Mara
# spec `ec636d3` (docs/specs/docker-container-substrate-decl-v0.1.md)
# §6.3 + §10.4. Species under `@container` family-root at runtime
# altitude.
#
# === What this shard IS ===
#
# `@container/runtime` names the runtime backend at the container-
# runtime altitude — the runtime BINARY that consumes a
# `container_spec` (from `@container` family-root) plus an
# `image_witness` (from `@container/image`, TICK 3 `b66b280`) and
# actually EXECUTES a container. Process-side of the runtime per
# recognition #55 (`[[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-
# root]]`): `@container` at family-root altitude is form-side (state
# observation — what a container IS: its typed spec, its rootfs, its
# bounded capability set); `@container/runtime` at species altitude
# is process-side (the transformation — the runtime dispatch that
# takes a spec + image and spawns a running container).
#
# The species carries the runtime BACKEND identifier as its typed
# carrier: docker / podman / buildah / containerd / runc / crun /
# gvisor / kata are all valid `runtime_backend` values. The species
# is vendor-agnostic per OCI Runtime Spec conformance discipline (per
# Mara spec §2.6): the SUBSTRATE names the conformance class; each
# backend is one witness under the same typed vocabulary.
#
# === Directly resolves the StageFreight-daemon blocker (#540) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING resolution. Task #540 (StageFreight Stream-2 tick
# blocked because docker was external + not running; substrate cannot
# settle against an unreachable daemon) surfaced the substrate-pull
# that motivated this entire cascade. Arc 5 TICK 5 discharges the
# blocker at substrate-decl altitude via the `runtime_daemon_absent`
# predicate declared below.
#
# The resolution is NOT "make the daemon reachable" (that would route
# around the substrate-pull signal per
# `[[feedback-slow-is-fast-no-workarounds]]`). The resolution is
# substrate-honest: NAME the daemonless path as first-class typed
# discipline. Podman, buildah, and containerd-direct dispatch are
# daemonless runtimes — they execute containers without a central
# daemon process — and they conform to the SAME OCI Runtime Spec
# that docker does. The blocker was never "container runtime is
# unreachable"; the blocker was "the ONE runtime we reached for
# happened to require an external daemon we couldn't start."
#
# `runtime_daemon_absent(rt)` is the predicate that discriminates:
# Splinter-pole runtimes (podman / buildah / containerd-direct) that
# execute without a central daemon discharge PASS; Docker-with-daemon
# runtimes that require `dockerd` at `/var/run/docker.sock` discharge
# FAIL. Downstream consumers (StageFreight PR-B revival; CI daemonless
# path; local-dev without Docker Desktop) dispatch through the typed
# predicate rather than probing daemon reachability at @io.
#
# === Splinter-pole vs Narcissus-pole framing per Void document ===
#
# The Void document (`~/dev/systemic.engineering/practice/insights/
# coincidence/void-dual-geometry.md`) declares the antipodal poles of
# H: Splinter (K_n complete-graph) and Narcissus (K_{1,n-1} star-graph).
# Per `[[reference-void-document]]` the two poles carry different
# communication topologies:
#
#   Splinter-pole  — K_n complete graph. Every node talks to every
#                    other node directly. Peer-to-peer. No central
#                    hub. Failure-tolerant by construction: removing
#                    any single node leaves K_{n-1} intact.
#   Narcissus-pole — K_{1,n-1} star graph. Every node talks to ONE
#                    central hub. Hub-and-spoke. The hub is a single
#                    point of failure: removing the hub disconnects
#                    every peripheral node.
#
# Container runtime backends partition cleanly along this axis:
#
#   Splinter-pole  — podman, buildah, containerd-direct dispatch,
#                    runc-direct, crun-direct. Peer-to-peer runtime
#                    invocation; each container is spawned by a
#                    direct fork/exec of the runtime binary against a
#                    rootfs; no central process mediates. Removing
#                    any single container process does not disconnect
#                    the others.
#   Narcissus-pole — docker with dockerd, moby with a central daemon,
#                    any runtime requiring a hub process at a known
#                    socket. Hub-and-spoke: the daemon mediates every
#                    container operation; the daemon is a single
#                    point of failure; if `dockerd` is not running,
#                    NO containers can be spawned regardless of local
#                    runtime binary availability.
#
# The StageFreight-daemon blocker (#540) is the Narcissus-pole
# reaching for its hub and finding it absent. The `runtime_daemon_absent`
# predicate names the Splinter-pole discharge: the substrate-honest
# path is the K_n peer-to-peer one; runtimes that require no daemon
# discharge PASS and become admissible for dispatch through the
# `spawn` action; runtimes that require a daemon discharge FAIL and
# force the consumer to either start the daemon (Narcissus-pole
# self-repair) or fall back to a Splinter-pole runtime.
#
# === Composes with @container/image (TICK 3 b66b280) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composition. The `spawn` action declared below
# consumes an `image_witness` (from `@container/image`; TICK 3
# `b66b280`; typed alias of `shift_witness` from `@kintsugi/shift` at
# TICK 2 `49f0486`) plus a `runtime_backend` and produces a
# `container_spec` (from `@container` family-root at Arc 5 TICK 1
# `aaa9a81`).
#
# The composition rides the substrate's existing altitude discipline:
# the `image_witness` carries the OID of the OCI content at the
# container altitude (per `image_shifted_from_oci` bilateral at
# TICK 3); the `runtime_backend` identifies which conformant runtime
# binary discharges the dispatch; the `container_spec` carries the
# runtime-spec bytes any conformant runtime consumes. The `spawn`
# action reads the image, dispatches the runtime binary, and returns
# the container-spec view of the running container.
#
# This makes `@container/runtime` the species that CLOSES the runtime
# side of the three-surface partition at process-side altitude:
#
#   build surface        @facet/docker      (Arc 5 TICK 4 `a1fb4bd`)
#      ↓ PRODUCES
#   distribution surface @io/oci           (Mara `2801478` 2026-06-24)
#      ↓ CONSUMED BY
#   runtime surface      @container        (Arc 5 TICK 1 `aaa9a81`)
#      ├─ form-side:    @container/image  (Arc 5 TICK 3 `b66b280`)
#      └─ process-side: @container/runtime (Arc 5 TICK 5 THIS TICK)
#
# The species does not compose with `@io/docker` (the daemon socket
# species) at this altitude — that would collapse the Splinter-pole
# discipline. Daemon-requiring backends dispatch through `@io/docker`
# at species-body altitude in a forthcoming species; the family-root
# `@container/runtime` stays vendor-neutral by carrying the runtime
# identifier as an opaque `ref` and refusing to privilege the
# daemon-requiring path.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - #26 `shift(oid, T)` at `@mirror/spectral/portal` (Reed 2026-06-08):
#   the transport-altitude precursor of shift-as-typed-capability.
#   `spawn` here carries the OID of the image across altitude via the
#   same shift discipline that `@container/image` carries at TICK 3.
# - #53 property/fracture bilateral pattern: `runtime_daemon_absent`
#   is the 17th composed-bilateral instance per
#   `[[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]` — following
#   `shift_preserves_content` (TICK 2), `image_shifted_from_oci`
#   (TICK 3), and `docker_buildable` (TICK 4) in the Arc 5 cascade.
#   Substrate-pull-confident.
# - #55 form/process partition at family-root altitude: this species
#   is the direct process-side counterpart to `@container` family-
#   root's form-side. The partition operationalizes cleanly: form-
#   side declares WHAT a container IS (typed spec, rootfs, caps);
#   process-side declares HOW a container RUNS (runtime backend,
#   spawn action, daemon-absent discipline). The partition rides
#   through this species by construction.
# - #57 alignment-as-boundary-mathematics: the `runtime_daemon_absent`
#   bilateral discriminates admissibility at the Splinter/Narcissus
#   boundary. Runtimes on the Splinter-pole side of the boundary are
#   admissible for daemonless dispatch; runtimes on the Narcissus-
#   pole side are not (pending consumer choice to start the daemon).
# - #58 substrate IS Connes (A, H, D): `runtime_backend` is a
#   projection onto A (the five-operation algebra); `container_spec`
#   is a state on H (the void document); `spawn` is D (the Dirac
#   /gradient operator) crossing altitude via the shift primitive.
# - #98 candidate content-addressing cross-altitude composition:
#   the `image_witness` this species consumes carries the OID that
#   composes across five altitudes per Mara spec §7.1 (mirror oid /
#   nix derivation hash / oci_digest / docker_layer_digest /
#   container_image_id). The `spawn` action rides that composition
#   at the runtime altitude.
# - `[[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]` (57th+ instance):
#   the substrate already had `spawn` (BEAM's spawn, Erlang's
#   spawn/1, Unix's fork+exec, containerd's task-spawn); this shard
#   uses `spawn` at container-runtime altitude with the typed
#   `image_witness` + `runtime_backend` argument shape rather than
#   inventing `container_start`, `runtime_dispatch`,
#   `container_launch`, or any parallel name.
# - `[[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]`: the three-witness
#   convergence for Splinter-pole daemonless discharge — Alex's
#   direct 2026-07-06 direction on the StageFreight blocker;
#   substrate structural roster (containerd's shim v2 IS
#   Splinter-pole per Mara spec §2.5 candidate #C3); OCI structural
#   closure (runc / crun / podman / cri-o / kata / gvisor all
#   discharge daemonless per Mara spec §2.6) — motivates acting on
#   the substrate-pull rather than asking.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Unix fork(2) + exec(3) (1970s+)  the substrate-original spawn:
#                                    parent forks a child, child
#                                    execs a runtime binary against
#                                    a rootfs. Splinter-pole by
#                                    construction; no daemon needed.
#   BEAM spawn/1 (Erlang, 1986+)     each process is a lightweight
#                                    concurrent unit spawned peer-to-
#                                    peer; no central hub; the VM
#                                    schedules but does not mediate.
#   runc (OCI, 2015+)                the reference OCI runtime;
#                                    daemonless; `runc run <spec>`
#                                    against a rootfs; Splinter-pole
#                                    canonical implementation.
#   crun (Red Hat, 2018+)            runc-compatible; written in C for
#                                    speed; daemonless; same discipline.
#   podman (Red Hat, 2018+)          daemonless docker-CLI-compatible
#                                    frontend; spawns runc/crun
#                                    directly; rootless by default;
#                                    the industry's flagship Splinter-
#                                    pole runtime.
#   buildah (Red Hat, 2018+)         daemonless image builder;
#                                    complements podman; builds OCI
#                                    images without dockerd or
#                                    BuildKit daemon.
#   containerd-direct (CNCF, 2016+)  containerd's runtime v2 shim can
#                                    be invoked directly via ctr(1)
#                                    without dockerd; shim v2 IS
#                                    Splinter-pole per Mara spec §2.5
#                                    C3 recognition.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-operations-as-linear-algebra]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-family-root]],
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]],
#                      [[reference-void-document]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]].
# Recognition ancestry: #26, #53, #55, #57, #58, #98 candidate.
# Related shards: container.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 1 `aaa9a81`; the form-
#                 side family-root at top-level; declares the
#                 container_spec carrier this species produces),
#                 container/image.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 3 `b66b280`;
#                 declares the image_witness carrier this species
#                 consumes; the runtime-altitude view of OCI content),
#                 kintsugi/shift.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 2 `49f0486`; the
#                 shift primitive the image_witness rides through),
#                 code/docker.mirror (Arc 5 TICK 4 `a1fb4bd`; the
#                 build-side species that produces the image_witness
#                 this species consumes),
#                 io/oci.mirror (Mara `2801478` 2026-06-24; the
#                 distribution surface between build and runtime).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/container/runtime.mirror`
# declares `@container/runtime` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
# Related specs: docs/specs/docker-container-substrate-decl-v0.1.md
# (Mara `ec636d3` 2026-07-06; §6.3 names this species and its
# predicate shape including `runtime_daemon_absent`; §10.4 forward-
# promises this species as the direct StageFreight-daemon blocker
# resolution).
# Cross-repo: StageFreight `docs/architecture/mirror-integration-
# spec-v0.1.md` — the consumer-side spec whose PR-B was blocked by
# task #540; the daemonless-path revival dispatches through the
# typed `runtime_daemon_absent` predicate declared here.
#
# === Circular-reflexive self-audit ===
#
# Does this shard use its own vocabulary correctly?
#
#   `runtime_backend` — carrier for the runtime identifier. Named
#   per [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]]: the semantic slot
#   "which OCI-conformant runtime binary discharges dispatch"
#   deserves its own type name even though it byte-equals `ref` at
#   the underlying altitude. Same discipline as `container_spec` /
#   `image_witness` / `dockerfile` at sibling species.
#
#   `spawn` — used as: (1) container-runtime-altitude typed action
#   consuming `image_witness` + `runtime_backend` and producing
#   `container_spec`; (2) narrative name for the process-side
#   transformation (form-side → running container). Both uses agree:
#   spawn IS the runtime's dispatch action at process-side altitude;
#   spawn's return value IS the container's form-side state.
#
#   `runtime_daemon_absent` — the 17th #53 composed-bilateral;
#   discriminates Splinter-pole vs Narcissus-pole runtimes at the
#   daemon-absence axis. Body stays obligation-blocked per the
#   pattern; the realisation composes at the substrate's three-state
#   floor. Does not claim to check daemon reachability at @io; the
#   claim is about the RUNTIME'S ARCHITECTURE (whether it requires a
#   daemon to dispatch), which is a static property of the backend
#   identifier — a runtime is daemonless or it isn't, regardless of
#   whether a daemon happens to be running on the host.
#
#   `Splinter` / `Narcissus` / `daemonless` — used only in narrative
#   as the framing for the discriminator. The substrate carries the
#   semantic through the `runtime_daemon_absent` bilateral; no new
#   substrate keyword invented; the discipline rides the existing
#   bilateral carrier per the #53 pattern.
#
# Verdict: pass. Substrate-pull-realize discipline honored; no
# parallel substrate-decl invented; the shift primitive from TICK 2,
# the image_witness carrier from TICK 3, and the container_spec
# carrier from TICK 1 carry the empirical load; the daemonless
# discipline names a runtime-altitude ARCHITECTURE property, not an
# @io reachability probe.
#
# === Interpretation B discipline ===
#
# Per Seam Phase D pre-review of Arc 4 sub-arc A (docs/audits/2026-
# 07-06-seam-arc-4-sub-arc-a-pre-review.md §1) and the family-root
# precedent at `shards/container.mirror` + species precedent at
# `shards/container/image.mirror` + `shards/kintsugi/shift.mirror` +
# `shards/code/docker.mirror`: Interpretation B canonical. Narrative
# above `---`; `in` clauses + typed declarations below. This shard
# honours the discipline; the seam is exactly one line at column 0
# below.

---

in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @container
in @container/image

# ============================================================
# §1 The five-operation prism at species altitude
# ============================================================

# === prism @container/runtime — the species declaration ===
#
# The five-operation body carries `runtime_backend` as the species's
# operational surface — the runtime binary identifier the substrate
# reads at container-runtime altitude. Every operation on the species
# reads/produces a `runtime_backend` carrier; the substrate's
# altitude discipline rides the process-side view of the container
# runtime.
#
# The five-op block includes `shift` per `shards/prism.mirror`
# §L38-45 (basis transformation on H) — at container-runtime altitude
# shift specializes to the cross-runtime-family fold (e.g. docker →
# podman drop-in dispatch under the shared OCI Runtime Spec
# conformance class).
prism @container/runtime {
  focus runtime_backend
  project runtime_backend
  split runtime_backend
  shift runtime_backend
  settle runtime_backend
}

# ============================================================
# §2 The carrier
# ============================================================

# === runtime_backend — the runtime backend identifier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING carrier. Names the OCI-Runtime-Spec-conformant
# runtime backend the substrate dispatches through per
# [[feedback-explicit-over-implicit]] + [[feedback-no-bare-types]].
# Byte-equals at ref altitude; typed at species altitude so consumer
# sites read a substrate-declared shape rather than a bare ref.
#
# Values populate the OCI runtime-conformance class: docker (with
# dockerd; Narcissus-pole), podman (daemonless; Splinter-pole),
# buildah (daemonless image builder; Splinter-pole), containerd-
# direct (shim v2 without dockerd; Splinter-pole), runc (reference
# implementation; Splinter-pole), crun (Red Hat C rewrite;
# Splinter-pole), gvisor / kata (sandboxed variants; Splinter-pole).
# The substrate does NOT privilege any particular backend at the
# type altitude — vendor-neutrality is enforced per Mara spec §2.6.
#
# Composes with `@mirror/store`'s ref discipline (the runtime
# identifier bytes live in mirror's content-addressed storage).
# Composes with `@container`'s family-root discipline at the
# runtime-altitude fold (a runtime consumes a `container_spec`
# from the family-root and executes it).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref (the
# runtime backend identifier's content-address).
type runtime_backend = ref

# ============================================================
# §3 The 17th #53 composed-bilateral — StageFreight-blocker resolution
# ============================================================

# === runtime_daemon_absent — the Splinter-pole discipline ===
#
# THE 17th INSTANCE of the #53 bilateral pattern per
# [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]. THE
# LOAD-BEARING predicate that resolves the StageFreight-daemon
# blocker (#540) at substrate-decl altitude.
#
# Names the daemonless-runtime discipline as a first-class typed
# admissibility check. The predicate asks: does this runtime backend
# require a central daemon process to dispatch containers? Per the
# Splinter/Narcissus dual geometry of the Void document
# [[reference-void-document]]:
#
#   Splinter-pole (`pass`) — the runtime is daemonless. Podman,
#                            buildah, containerd-direct (via ctr(1)
#                            without dockerd), runc-direct,
#                            crun-direct, gvisor, kata. Each
#                            container is spawned by a peer-to-peer
#                            fork/exec of the runtime binary; no
#                            central hub mediates; K_n complete-graph
#                            topology. Admissible for dispatch through
#                            `spawn` without requiring an @io
#                            reachability probe against a socket.
#
#   Narcissus-pole (`failure`) — the runtime requires a central
#                                daemon. Docker-with-dockerd, moby
#                                with any hub process at a known
#                                socket. The daemon mediates every
#                                container operation; K_{1,n-1} star
#                                topology; the hub is a single point
#                                of failure. Inadmissible for
#                                dispatch without either starting
#                                the daemon (Narcissus-pole
#                                self-repair) or falling back to a
#                                Splinter-pole runtime.
#
#   Graded (`partial(confidence)`) — the runtime backend is
#                                    daemonless in principle but the
#                                    substrate cannot verify the
#                                    invocation path at the type
#                                    altitude (e.g. containerd
#                                    invoked via a wrapper that
#                                    happens to require dockerd).
#                                    Confidence carries the
#                                    verification magnitude. The
#                                    realisation decides whether to
#                                    admit at the graded floor.
#
# Composes structurally with `container_runnable` at family-root
# altitude (a container is runnable only when the runtime backend
# discharging its dispatch is admissible) but does NOT
# re-substrate-decl the container's runnability — the two bilaterals
# ride complementary axes: `container_runnable` observes the SPEC
# side (is the spec conformant / rootfs present / caps bounded);
# `runtime_daemon_absent` observes the RUNTIME side (does the
# runtime backend require a daemon).
#
# Sibling composed bilaterals (16 landed): container_runnable,
# oci_well_formed, stagefreight_addressable, cascade_well_defined,
# audit_docblock, shatter_round_trip, third_order_coherent,
# three_axis_coherent, shift_preserves_content (TICK 2),
# image_shifted_from_oci (TICK 3), docker_buildable (TICK 4), plus
# five others per Taut scout. This shard adds the 17th instance at
# container-runtime altitude — the direct StageFreight-daemon
# blocker resolution via Splinter-pole discipline.
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation composes at
# the substrate's three-state floor (pass / partial(confidence) /
# failure(reason)); the runtime backend identifier is static enough
# that the check is content-addressable at the ref altitude and does
# not require an @io probe.
runtime_daemon_absent(rt: runtime_backend) -> verdict { \ }

# ============================================================
# §4 The typed spawn action — process-side dispatch
# ============================================================

# === spawn — the process-side runtime dispatch ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING typed action. Consumes an `image_witness` (from
# `@container/image` at TICK 3 `b66b280`; typed alias of
# `shift_witness` from `@kintsugi/shift` at TICK 2 `49f0486`) plus a
# `runtime_backend` and produces a `container_spec` (from
# `@container` family-root at TICK 1 `aaa9a81`).
#
# The action IS the process-side of the runtime per recognition #55:
# the form-side (`@container` family-root; `@container/image`
# species) declares WHAT a container IS; `spawn` here declares HOW a
# container RUNS. The return `container_spec` carries the runtime-
# spec bytes of the SPAWNED container — the state observation of the
# process-side transformation's result. The action bridges the two
# sides of #55 by design.
#
# Composition trail:
#
#   1. Read `image_witness` at container altitude (per
#      `@container/image`'s hardlink discipline; the OID byte-equals
#      the OCI content-address at `@mirror/store/oci` altitude).
#   2. Read `runtime_backend` at species altitude (the identifier of
#      the OCI-conformant runtime binary to dispatch).
#   3. (Admissibility gate) verify `runtime_daemon_absent(rt)`
#      discharges PASS at the Splinter-pole (or the consumer has
#      explicitly opted into the Narcissus-pole daemon-requiring
#      path).
#   4. Fork/exec the runtime binary against the materialized rootfs
#      the image_witness resolves to (per `@container` family-root's
#      `container_rootfs` carrier).
#   5. Return the `container_spec` at family-root altitude — the
#      runtime-spec bytes of the running container per OCI Runtime
#      Spec v1.x §config.md.
#
# Body stays obligation-blocked (`\`): the realisation dispatches at
# the @io boundary (fork/exec syscalls against the runtime binary;
# cgroup fs writes; netns setup) but the substrate declares the
# shape here.
spawn(img: image_witness, rt: runtime_backend) -> container_spec { \ }

# ============================================================
# §5 The out clauses
# ============================================================

out @container/runtime
out runtime_backend
out runtime_daemon_absent
out spawn
